{"seq":18,"trial_id":"v03-opus-dev-2026-10/hermes-opus-gbrain-told-company-mu-v03-dev/sy-01-quarrendon-ticket-numbers/r3","wall_ts":"2026-11-01T09:42:46.527Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:10:00-05:00","args_digest":"4241d24181ade2579b314cf98737dba03d40e2bcc6e303430e518ae767aa09b9","actor":"assistant","via":"mcp","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DV03OPU0001","text":"Hi Dana, I went through all six of Moss's notes in the shared team digests. Four mention Quarrendon Freight Lines, and only two of those have a ticket number:\n\n1. #PD-4492, from \"Moss: Sunday prep for Ruth\" (teams/team-north/digests/2025-10-05-north-sunday.md). Thea Ramaswell opened it on 4 Oct 2025 because drivers at Dock Doors 14-18 in the Eau Claire yard weren't getting SMS bay assignments. Support patched it that evening, and Thea confirmed the 5 Oct 04:00 shift got through fine. Moss also noted the kiosk logs should be archived before the 14 Oct 2025 maintenance window.\n\n2. #4419, from \"Moss: North cheat sheet (undated)\" (teams/team-north/digests/north-account-cheatsheet.md). It says Thea logged this one for gatehouse barcode scanners not reading trailer tags at Door 14 on third shift, and that it was escalated to tier-2 for scanner firmware testing. One caution: other notes describe #4419 differently. Ilse's May 2025 handoff email calls it a Duluth Gate 3 kiosk glitch, and Marcus's July 2025 wrap-up calls it Gate 3 printer lag. Check the actual ticket before you quote Moss's description.\n\nThe other two Moss notes about QFL have no ticket numbers: the 14 Sep 2025 pipeline digest and the 23 Mar 2026 renewal check-in. The tickets in the Central handoff digest (#4409, #4412, FR-882) belong to Marrow accounts, not QFL.\n\nOther QFL tickets show up in North weeklies and other files, but not in Moss's notes. If you want those for the weekly too, I can list them."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DV03OPU0001","ts":"1791987000.000124"}}
